---
description: Unify AI architecture guardrails
alwaysApply: true
---

You are working on Unify AI, an iOS Swift/Xcode app with local LLM runtime and Secretary/Exchange mode.

Core constraints:
- Do not replace the architecture unless explicitly asked.
- Do not create parallel canonical types when existing canonical types exist.
- Prefer small paste-over patches.
- Preserve local/offline/on-device assumptions.
- Preserve privacy-first behavior.
- Avoid cloud API assumptions.
- Avoid fake async/background promises.
- Do not remove existing persistence, runtime, or safety boundaries.

Secretary / Exchange architecture:
- ExchangeIntent and ExchangeIntentFacets are canonical. Do not create replacement intent/facet files.
- ExchangeThread is the durable source of truth for thread state.
- ExchangeFacade is the UI-facing API.
- ExchangeThreadEngine should own thread lifecycle mutations.
- ExchangeOrchestrator coordinates thread flow.
- UI should render from canonical snapshots, not mixed stale fields.

Runtime architecture:
- Preserve runtime-owned conversation direction.
- Avoid rebuilding full prompt every turn.
- Prefer scaffold + warm incremental turns.
- Keep memory augmentation small, relevant, and late.
- Do not block real user generation on prewarm.
- Be careful with iOS background/foreground lifecycle.

Coding style:
- SwiftUI views should remain readable and compositional.
- Prefer explicit state ownership over clever callbacks.
- When changing callbacks, inspect parent and child call sites.
- Avoid broad renames unless requested.
- For fixes, provide per-function paste-over blocks when possible.